  "Onderdeel: tabbladen (CnTabs)": "Component: tabs (CnTabs)",
  "Tabs: the folder strip": "",
  "One tab strip for every detail page. It is the CnTabs component from nextcloud-vue, drawn in the Zuiddrecht tokens: the open tab shares the white of the card below it, bold, with no line under it; the closed tabs sit on a darker surface, and the Actions menu stands at the right end of the strip, outside the row of tabs.": "",
  "Anatomy": "",
  "The panel is the card itself. The open tab has no line under it, so tab and card read as one sheet.": "",
  "Closed tab.": "",
  "Darker surface #ECEEF1 with its own edge, regular weight, 8 px top corners. The whole strip reads as a control at a glance.": "",
  "Open tab.": "",
  "White like the card, bold label, no line under it: the tab overlaps the card by 1 px and covers its top edge, so tab and card read as one sheet. No coloured edge: white and bold already carry the selection.": "",
  "Strip.": "",
  "No line of its own. The only line is the card's top edge, which ends in the card's rounded top right corner, never past it.": "",
  "Actions.": "",
  "The secondary button, outside the tablist. A screen reader counting four tabs hears four, not five.": "",
  "Panel.": "",
  "The card with its full border, square only at the top left under the first tab. Inactive panels stay in the DOM, hidden, so a tab switch is instant.": "",
  "States": "",
  "Rest": "",
  "Hover": "",
  "Focus": "",
  "Disabled": "",
  "Selection lives in the surface and the weight, never in colour alone. In forced-colours mode, where backgrounds disappear, the bold label and the missing bottom line still tell the open tab apart.": "",
  "Many tabs wrap, they never scroll": "",
  "Documents": "",
  "Parties": "",
  "Publication": "",
  "Notes": "",
  "A second row keeps every tab reachable without a gesture. Actions stays on the first row, top-aligned, so it reads as the strip's control and not as the last tab's.": "",
  "What thematiq sets for the Zuiddrecht set, and the Nextcloud variable CnTabs reads.": "",
