  "34 px, 8 px 12 px": "",
  "Corners": "",
  "8 px top": "",
  "Tabs hold parallel views of one object: details, contact moments, related items, decisions. They never hide the next step; that stays in the What now card above the strip.": "",
  "One Actions menu per strip, in the nav-end slot. A panel never draws its own header with a second menu.": "",
  "A count sits in a small grey circle after the label, so it never reads as part of the title, and it follows the data.": "",
  "An icon is optional and sits before the label at 16 px. Icon-only tabs are not allowed.": "",
  "The segmented control drawn on the earlier case page is retired for page sections. It stays for a true either-or, such as list and board on an overview.": "",
  "Keyboard: Left and Right move between tabs, Home and End jump to the ends, only the open tab is in the Tab order. The component already does this; the design never asks for anything else.": ""
